 {
  "summary": "The frozen ~ merges two different pen marks. On the page 5-like strokes occur only where a letter must be withdrawn (11 groups) and c-with-tail hooks only where a letter must be doubled (5 groups, including the signature). No group crosses over. Arrow-like marks: 11 groups, all nouns or a pronoun needing plural/genitive. Filled marks: 8 groups including 966, 7 fit past on a verb, 1 (70) fails on the key value. No third-person verb occurs, so that half of the rule is untested. Shape caveat: the mark assignments are functional; on the page the plural sign is arrow-like and the past sign is a filled diamond-like blob, which is the reverse of the printed shape names as relayed to me."
 }
]